From: =?UTF-8?q?Samuel=20Carre=C3=B1o?= <soyminero11yt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:28:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] fix: survive the keyring daemon being replaced while
 Postcard runs

libsecret keeps a proxy to the Secret Service it first talked to. After
gnome-keyring-daemon is replaced (--replace, a crash, a restart) every
lookup on that proxy fails with "The name :1.N was not provided by any
.service files" for the rest of the process's life. The sync worker did
not catch that: the thread died with its account still marked as
syncing, so every later sync (the poll, the inbox watchers, Refresh)
was dropped as "already running" and new mail never arrived again.

- secrets: run each libsecret call through _keyring(), which drops the
  cached proxy (Secret.Service.disconnect) and retries once on a D-Bus
  error; credential_for returns None if the keyring is still unreachable.
- window: the sync worker reports an exception from credential_for
  (an OAuth refresh with the network gone raises too) through
  errors.classify like a failed fetch; the flag, move, body and outbox
  workers fall back to their "no credential" path instead of dying.
- tests for the retry and the None fallback.
